what's the right business model hello  everyone welcome to the TGIM or answer a  question for one of my mastermind group  members in our online mastermind group I  am coming to you from New Orleans today  I'm doing this presentation tomorrow and  the next day and I am lying on my hotel  bed and answering the questions because  I want to help my group and this is a  great question that came in so one of my  master my members has a YouTube channel  she has 13 videos that she's done in two  months I believe she's making almost  nothing on her channel and she's  wondering what's the right business  model how do I get this going I don't  want to have to go get a job how do i  turn this into a full time income that  that I can continue to follow my passion  and be really successful with and I'm  gonna throw a curveball I'm gonna do  something that I think is against the  traditional advice that you may get as  much as I love business models and  figuring out a plan ah there's such a  thing as over planning at the start and  the funny thing is the plan that you  start with is rarely going to be the  plan that you end with and I learned  this lesson the hard way when I was 21  22 and I thought I had the perfect plan  for my software company and and it  wasn't the right plan and I missed out  on a 40 million dollar deal because of  it because I was too slow to react  because I was so busy trying to find the  perfect plan that I wasn't actually  paying attention to what was happening  in the market and I lost a huge deal and  so 40 million dollar deal when you're 20  21 22 that's a that's an expensive  lesson to learn the one that I've  carried with me for the rest of my  career so far here's what happens okay I  see this a lot on YouTube and I says lot  with startup entrepreneurs web-based  entrepreneurs you you look at all the  models and there's nothing wrong with  looking all the mall you say okay you  know what I'm going to create a patreon  campaign I'm going to create a t-shirt  line I'm going to launch an e-book  whatever it is and then you're still  we're going to youtube channel but then  you divert some of your attention so you  can focus on the landing pages and the  products and everything else that you're  trying to create and so see you're  creating the land  page for a patreon campaign okay and you  know it doesn't it doesn't do well you  put it out there it doesn't do well and  then you think ok well my headline  didn't work right or the way I market it  didn't work or something else you can  bring yourself with another reason so  then you take more time again away from  doing stuff on your YouTube channel and  invest it on this and then you launch it  and again it doesn't work surprised it  doesn't work and and it's super  frustrating you think maybe I should  give up maybe maybe that I'm not meant  to make any money from this maybe I know  I don't have the right plan and the  problem was never with the plan the  problem was the honest truth is you  don't have an audience that cares yet  that's like the heart like hit me in the  heart and twist it like over and over  and over comment but its true like you  don't have an audience that cares enough  to buy a t-shirt line from you to donate  to a patreon campaign to buy your ebook  or whatever other business model you're  trying to make outside of Adsense your  audience doesn't care enough about you  yet because you haven't invested the  time to make an amazing contribution to  the community so they care about you  because you're diverting your attention  away from making great videos to try to  monetize them and create a business  model too soon and so my favorite way of  doing it is let your audience take you  where they want to go and see if that's  aligned with you so an example comes  from a great video that was on Tim  Schmoyer his channel not too long ago  where is with the podcast answer man  this guy is like the Guru of podcasting  and he started off in podcasting and he  had his podcast and put a ton of love  into it in a regular series and then  people started asking him hey do you do  you do consulting because I want to do  my own podcast and and I'd love some  help and so we said sure yeah sure I'll  do consulting why not and so he started  his consulting business and then as I  started doing consulting he realized one  day that he was training he had like  three or four calls back to back and  they're all about how to use a certain  Adobe product to help create and edit  the show afterwards and he basically  took somebody from scratch  having to knowing how to use it and then  he had to do it for the Mexico from  scratch to knowing how to use it for  their podcast and then one more time  taking from scratch to know how to use  it the next time and this this is  ridiculous like this isn't fun for me  I'm answering the same thing over and  over and over and over and over again  and then the light bulb went off you  know I should turn this into a product  and that became one of his best selling  products and that's how he got into the  product business so he started off doing  what he loved his community came to him  and said hey we want we need consulting  will you do this for us and he built it  and then he took the consulting clients  who are paying him and turned that into  products based on what they were asking  for and so that's what I've encouraged  you to do I would encourage you to put  more love into your YouTube channel  because 13 videos in two months it's not  enough it's like you want to turn this  into a full-time a career you want to  make some serious money from this you  got to be doing it once a day you got to  find a way to do it once a day get more  content up there and if you have to go  take a job on the side part time to  support this passion of yours and this  is where you want to go and do it do  whatever you need to do to get that  happening build up your audience put a  lot of love into it and wait for them to  come up with ideas people say hey you  know people write to me and say hey I'd  love to donate to use our way to do it  migrate a patreon campaign people saw  some of the quotes that I had said  that'd be a great t-shirt so we created  a t-shirt line but even that's on a  small scale that's not even doing  massively well for me either people ask  me if I did consulting and so I created  the mastermind group uh you know brands  found me and they said hey Evan we'd  love to have you sage why am I here  right they found me on social media  because I've been pulling tons of love  into it and they asked me to come and  speak at their event i'm doing an event  i'm speaking tomorrow i speak at their  next day and so that's why i encourage  you to do is pour tons more love into  the channel kick up a ton of noise and  then let your audience take you where  they want to go and see is that align  with what you want to do and i think  you'll have a lot more success I think  you'll have a lot more fun doing the  stuff you want to do I think you have a  lot more a lot less stress trying to  figure out what the perfect model is  and I think it allows you to be flexible  in in being able to follow what the  market wants instead of you trying to  predict where it's going because your  prediction is always going to be wrong  and it's way better to listen to your  customers and go with them so that's my  advice little curve ball today from  Monday night but hopefully that helps  and looking forward to seeing how you do  this month take care everybody
 

